846: - <a id="decided-project-infoflow-2026-11-06"></a>**Secrets, noninterference and constant time**
847:   (owner, 2026-11-06: "a", option (a) on every question of the [proposal](archive/crucial-2026-11-06/INFOFLOW.md), reviewed
848:   by Codex, agy and Kimi). Noninterference and constant time are two separate claims (authority
849:   rule 14), each a theorem about the source semantics of every accepted program, holding at the
850:   binary only under named backend premises. The surface is the type `Secret<T>`, with `classify`,
851:   `declassify(x, "reason")`, `ct_select` and `ct_eq`; a `declassify` is traced in the facts like a
852:   `#[may_not_terminate]` permission. Control flow on a secret is refused (write `ct_select`);
853:   container lengths are public, and a secret length is refused. `Secret<T>` is `Copy` only for
854:   scalar `T`; secret arrays and heap secrets are linear and wiped on destroy, which revises
855:   [Q2.2](#q2-2-revision). The observer model is the baseline constant-time model (branches, exact
856:   addresses, variable-time operations); speculative leakage is not covered. The leakage-trace
857:   interface is fixed in A2i (R-0592); `Secret<T>` lands as its own slice with its proofs (R-0596).
858:   Its sources include the pure `classify` of a value passed in; grant-backed sources come with the
859:   console, files and network ([vertical slices](#decided-project-vertical-slices-2026-11-06)).
860:   Revised 2026-11-07 by the [randomness decision](#decided-2026-11-07-stack-randomness): the entropy capability arrives at slice 6, yields
